{"id": "imdb-001", "level": "noob", "nl_description": "I want to make a databse to keep track of movies and tv shows. Each movie or show has a name (and maybe a difrent original name), the year it came out, how long it is in minuts, and what jenre it is (like action or comedy). Some shows ran for multipul years so they have a start and end year. Also I want to store ratins -- like an average score from 1 to 10 and how many people voted on it. The more populer a movie is the more votes it usualy has, so there will be a huge range in vote counts. Most movies are between like 70 and 120 minuts long.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "original_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_adult", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "end_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "runtime_minutes", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "genres", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_RATING", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "average_rating", "data_type": "DECIMAL"}, {"name": "num_votes", "data_type": "INT"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_RATING", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"TITLE_RATING.average_rating": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 7.0, "std": 1.3}}, "TITLE_RATING.num_votes": {"family": "lognormal", "params": {"mu": 5.5, "sigma": 2.0}}, "TITLE_BASIC.runtime_minutes": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 90.0, "std": 30.0}}}}
{"id": "imdb-002", "level": "noob", "nl_description": "My freind wants a database for a movie website. People in the movie industry have a name, the year they were born, when they died if applicable, and a main job like actor or director. They are conected to movies -- each movie credits multipul people with diffrent roles. The billing order matters (like first billed actor is most importent). Some people are both actors and writers so they can have more than one proffesion. Movies have a title and release year. Actors born way back in the 1800s are in there too, all the way up to recent years.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "NAME_BASIC", "pk": "nconst", "columns": [{"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_name", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "birth_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "death_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "primary_profession", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "known_for_titles", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "job", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "characters", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "nconst", "referred_table": "NAME_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"NAME_BASIC.birth_year": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1850.0, "high": 2005.0}}, "TITLE_PRINCIPAL.ordering": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1.0, "high": 10.0}}}}
{"id": "imdb-003", "level": "intermediate", "nl_description": "Design a database for an entertainment metadata platform covering movies, TV series, and short films. Titles have a type (movie, series, short, video game, etc.), primary and original names, content rating flag, a start and optionally an end year, runtime in minutes, and a comma-separated genre list. Ratings data is separate: each rated title gets a floating point average score between 1 and 10 and an integer vote count. TV series have nested episode records -- each episode links back to its parent series and carries a season number and episode number. People in the industry have a unique identifier, a full name, birth and death years, and listed professions. Each title credits principals in an ordered list -- the record contains the person, their role category, a free-text job description, and the characters they played (stored as a JSON array string for actors). The title is the central entity that ratings, episodes, and principals all hang off.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "original_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_adult", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "end_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "runtime_minutes", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "genres", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_RATING", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "average_rating", "data_type": "DECIMAL"}, {"name": "num_votes", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_EPISODE", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "parent_tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "season_number", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "episode_number", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "NAME_BASIC", "pk": "nconst", "columns": [{"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_name", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "birth_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "death_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "primary_profession", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "known_for_titles", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "job", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "characters", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_RATING", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "parent_tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "nconst", "referred_table": "NAME_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"TITLE_RATING.average_rating": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 7.0, "std": 1.3}}, "TITLE_RATING.num_votes": {"family": "lognormal", "params": {"mu": 5.5, "sigma": 2.0}}, "TITLE_BASIC.runtime_minutes": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 90.0, "std": 30.0}}, "NAME_BASIC.birth_year": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1850.0, "high": 2005.0}}}}
{"id": "imdb-004", "level": "intermediate", "nl_description": "We need a schema for a global entertainment catalog. Films and series have official titles and may have separate original-language titles that differ. Alternate release titles are tracked per region and language -- a title can have many alternate names with different locales, types (working title, festival title, etc.) and an original title flag. Each alternate title has an ordering number within a title's set of aliases. People in the entertainment industry are the other core entity: each has unique identifiers, full name, year born, year of death if deceased, and their main professional roles. For titles where we want to track precise credits, there is a principals table with ordered billing positions linking people to titles with role categories. Separately, director and writer credits are stored in a concise crew table where each title row holds a comma-separated list of director identifiers and a separate list for writers. Crowdsourced ratings provide an average and a total vote count per title.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "original_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_adult", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "end_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "runtime_minutes", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "genres", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_RATING", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "average_rating", "data_type": "DECIMAL"}, {"name": "num_votes", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_AKA", "pk": "title_id", "columns": [{"name": "title_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "region", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "types", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "attributes", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_original_title", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "NAME_BASIC", "pk": "nconst", "columns": [{"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_name", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "birth_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "death_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "primary_profession", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "known_for_titles", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "job", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "characters", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_CREW", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "directors", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "writers", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_RATING", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_AKA", "referencing_column": "title_id", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "nconst", "referred_table": "NAME_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_CREW", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"TITLE_RATING.average_rating": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 7.0, "std": 1.3}}, "TITLE_RATING.num_votes": {"family": "lognormal", "params": {"mu": 5.5, "sigma": 2.0}}, "TITLE_BASIC.runtime_minutes": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 90.0, "std": 30.0}}, "NAME_BASIC.birth_year": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1850.0, "high": 2005.0}}}}
{"id": "imdb-005", "level": "expert", "nl_description": "Schema for a comprehensive public entertainment metadata repository containing approximately 10.7M title records and 13M name records. Central entity is the title, with a surrogate key in 'tt' prefix format. Title types include movie, short, tvSeries, tvEpisode, tvMiniSeries, tvMovie, tvShort, tvSpecial, video, and videoGame. Key attributes: primary and original title strings, adult content flag (boolean int), release start year, optional end year (for series and mini-series), runtime in minutes, and a denormalized multi-valued genres field (comma-delimited, max three genres). Ratings are a dependent entity with a 1:0-1 relationship to titles: floating point average on [1.0, 10.0] and integer vote count. Vote distribution is highly right-skewed: median title has ~250 votes, mean is in the thousands due to mass-voted titles. Runtime is approximately normally distributed around 90 minutes with std ~30, representing feature-length content; this is left-skewed slightly due to short films. Episode records form a self-referential structure on titles: each episode title points to a parent series title with a season and episode number (both nullable for unnumbered episodes). People dimension: nconst 'nm' prefix, name, birth year uniform in [1850, 2005], death year for deceased. Multi-valued profession field. Principal credits: title-person junction with ordering, role category, freetext job, and characters array. Crew table: denormalized director/writer lists per title.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "original_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_adult", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "end_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "runtime_minutes", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "genres", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_RATING", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "average_rating", "data_type": "DECIMAL"}, {"name": "num_votes", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_EPISODE", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "parent_tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "season_number", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "episode_number", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_AKA", "pk": "title_id", "columns": [{"name": "title_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "region", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "types", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "attributes", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_original_title", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "NAME_BASIC", "pk": "nconst", "columns": [{"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_name", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "birth_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "death_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "primary_profession", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "known_for_titles", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "job", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "characters", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_CREW", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "directors", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "writers", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_RATING", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "parent_tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_AKA", "referencing_column": "title_id", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "nconst", "referred_table": "NAME_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_CREW", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"TITLE_RATING.average_rating": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 7.0, "std": 1.3}}, "TITLE_RATING.num_votes": {"family": "lognormal", "params": {"mu": 5.5, "sigma": 2.0}}, "TITLE_BASIC.runtime_minutes": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 90.0, "std": 30.0}}, "NAME_BASIC.birth_year": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1850.0, "high": 2005.0}}, "TITLE_PRINCIPAL.ordering": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1.0, "high": 10.0}}}}
{"id": "imdb-006", "level": "expert", "nl_description": "Relational schema for a non-commercial entertainment industry data service. Title index has approximately 10M records spanning content from 1888 onwards. Type taxonomy: 10 distinct title types with distinct runtime profiles (feature films peak near 90min, shorts cluster under 40min, video games excluded from runtime). Title uniqueness: surrogate key is the canonical identifier; a title may have the same primary and original title string or differ (localization). The regional alias table creates a many-to-many between titles and locale-language pairs; each alias has a stable ordering number within its title, a type attribute distinguishing theatrical releases from alternate cuts or working titles, and an is_original flag marking the source-language entry. Name registry: ~13M people records with optional temporal bounds (birth/death years). Profession field is multi-valued (comma-separated, max 3). The 'knownForTitles' field cross-references the title index but is denormalized. Credits: principal ordering is billing priority (1 = top-billed); category field distinguishes acting roles from behind-camera ones; character names are JSON-encoded for actors. Crew table stores director and writer lists as comma-delimited identifier strings. Rating aggregates are immutable summaries of crowdsourced votes; only a subset of titles have ratings.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "TITLE_BASIC", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "title_type", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "original_title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_adult", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "start_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "end_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "runtime_minutes", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "genres", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_RATING", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "average_rating", "data_type": "DECIMAL"}, {"name": "num_votes", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_EPISODE", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "parent_tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "season_number", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "episode_number", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_AKA", "pk": "title_id", "columns": [{"name": "title_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "title", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "region", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "types", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "attributes", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "is_original_title", "data_type": "INT"}]}, {"name": "NAME_BASIC", "pk": "nconst", "columns": [{"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "primary_name", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "birth_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "death_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "primary_profession", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "known_for_titles", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ordering", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "nconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "category", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "job", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "characters", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "TITLE_CREW", "pk": "tconst", "columns": [{"name": "tconst", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "directors", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "writers", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}]}], "relationships": [{"referencing_table": "TITLE_RATING", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_EPISODE", "referencing_column": "parent_tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_AKA", "referencing_column": "title_id", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_PRINCIPAL", "referencing_column": "nconst", "referred_table": "NAME_BASIC"}, {"referencing_table": "TITLE_CREW", "referencing_column": "tconst", "referred_table": "TITLE_BASIC"}]}, "ground_truth_distributions": {"TITLE_RATING.average_rating": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 7.0, "std": 1.3}}, "TITLE_RATING.num_votes": {"family": "lognormal", "params": {"mu": 5.5, "sigma": 2.0}}, "TITLE_BASIC.runtime_minutes": {"family": "normal", "params": {"mean": 90.0, "std": 30.0}}, "NAME_BASIC.birth_year": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1850.0, "high": 2005.0}}, "TITLE_PRINCIPAL.ordering": {"family": "uniform", "params": {"low": 1.0, "high": 10.0}}}}
